('precise', '/pri''sais/', 'a. 精确的, 严谨的, 明确的 [机] 精密的, 正确的', 'adj', 'He gave me precise instructions to do the job.', '他给我的工作作出了明确指示。', 'CET4', 0),
('precision', '/pri''siʒәn/', 'n. 精密, 精确, 精确度, 精度 a. 精密的, 精确的 [计] 精度', 'n', 'Our teacher is someone who likes precision, and always demands precise answers of her students.', '老师性喜精准——她总是要求精确的答案。', 'CET4', 0),
